Blackdrift: run SearchMiddleware's engine loads one at a time.

Why: on a fresh install, 1 in 5 first launches crashed with
XmlPullParserException ("Expected start tag: END_DOCUMENT") in
CustomSearchEngineStorage.loadSearchEngine. RegionMiddleware dispatches
SetRegionAction twice on first launch (cached region, then the located one),
and each dispatch starts loadSearchEngines in parallel. Blackdrift's first-run
migration (focus-android 0207) saves the Startpage engine in one load, and
SearchEngineWriter writes straight into the final XML file (not through
AtomicFile), so the custom-engine listing in the other load can read a
half-written file. Upstream Focus has no first-run migration write, so it
rarely hits this; bug 1796453 ("Intermittent loadSearchEngineList
successfully loads after saving") is the nearest upstream report. A Mutex
around the load body (moved into loadSearchEnginesLocked) serialises the
loads, so the second one starts only after the first has saved and
listed. It also stops two overlapping loads from racing to set the state.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

